We thank you for your valuable reviews and address your concerns as follows.

**Q1**: *The comparison with state-of-the-art methods is limited to a few selected approaches. A more extensive comparison with a broader range of recent methods would strengthen the paper's contributions, such as SegNeuron.*

**A1**: Thanks for your suggestion, SegNeuron is an impressive work dedicated to generalized neuron segmentation, which is contemporary with our work. We have supplemented the comparison with SegNeuron on the AC3 dataset in the table below. **Note that one of the SegNeuron's training sets (*i.e.,* Kasthuri) contains AC3 (*i.e.,* our test set).** We found that even with this unfair comparison, SegNeuron achieved only slightly better VOI than ours. However, our method is 9 times faster than SegNeuron, demonstrating the strong efficiency advantage of our method.


